| `Timestamp` is a compiled-in core handler taking no operands: it reports
| the current Unix time in whole seconds. Like every core result it comes
| back as a particle — `TimestampResult` — not a bare number.
|
| The value is checked inside a block rather than left as a top-level
| binding: the assertion is the whole point, and keeping the timestamp out
| of top-level scope means the program prints nothing at all.
{
    emit Timestamp {} to core get t
    assert t._class = "TimestampResult"
    assert t.value ≥ 1700000000
}
